        "title": "Soil Chemistry: CEC, pH, Redox, Mineral Nutrients, Buffering",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Soil chemistry determines which nutrients are available to plants and microorganisms. Four interacting chemical systems govern this: cation exchange capacity (CEC, the nutrient holding capacity), soil pH (the master chemical variable controlling almost everything else), redox chemistry (controlling nutrient forms in wet soils), and specific nutrient chemistry (P sorption, Al toxicity, liming)."
    },
